   "description": "Gives trr and Qrr. The DUT source is on the positive Vdd line; its drain and gate meet at a node that runs through a current sensor (Isd) to the drain of an N-channel switch pulsed by Ig, and the inductor L returns that node to the positive Vdd line. On the waveforms, with the switch off the diode carries -IF; when the switch turns on the current falls at dI/dt, reverses to a peak -IRM and recovers over trr, and -Vds rises to Vdd. Qrr = -∫I dt over the reverse current. The recovery rows use IF = -14 A, dI/dt = 500 A/µs.",
